# R Tidyverse Workflow Rules

## Quarto-First
Every analysis starts as a Quarto document (.qmd). Code lives in named chunks. The document must render cleanly from scratch (`quarto render`) before it is considered done — no relying on objects in the global environment.

## Function Extraction Loop
Write analysis in a Quarto chunk → extract reusable logic into `R/` function → add testthat test → refactor Quarto to call the function. This keeps the document narrative-focused and the logic testable.

## renv Discipline
`renv::restore()` at the start of every session. `renv::snapshot()` after every `install.packages()` or `renv::install()`. The lockfile is the source of truth — not your personal library.

## Red-Green-Refactor (testthat)
Write a failing `test_that()` → implement the `R/` function → make it green. `testthat::test_dir("tests/testthat/")` must pass before committing.

## CI Gate
`lintr::lint_dir("R/")` → `styler::style_dir("R/", dry = "fail")` → `testthat::test_dir("tests/testthat/")` → `quarto render`. All steps pass on CI.

## Seed Discipline
Every script and test that uses randomness calls `set.seed(42)` (or project-defined seed from config) at the top. No unseeded random operations.
